son\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"b1c6f49614e106ea0875d354dbb3549d3fa1c64f92af66f300d0a83e08892097","event_uuid":"e9b137ce-c2de-4c9b-b51c-c7730dd77aa2","position":{"commit_sha":"7dd44de258bd63e685e728143ea0ff68634a3b57","position":"1795206531716795001-e9b137ce-c2de-4c9b-b51c-c7730dd77aa2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"082095bc0fa7334f7e7df55cebb860fc0cfbfd11b1e8e312e508fef1f6956e65","event_uuid":"db67674a-f13f-4942-b804-a77c75c0a567","position":{"commit_sha":"94e08b03e7c099c1a8956e53baf63fa534bc2f1f","position":"1795207993826171486-db67674a-f13f-4942-b804-a77c75c0a567"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Deterministic reproduction and fix evidence (2026-11-19, PST).\n\n**Reproduction (AC1).** PATH `git` shim that sleeps before any `update-ref`, then execs the real git, on origin/main 2ca3e28fcc6:\n- delay 4.5 s: `test_in_flight_refusal_clears_owned_pause_before_mutation` 2 passed.\n- delay 5.6 s: both parameters fail; `[doctor]`: `RefLockTimeoutError: git update-ref refs/reconciler/gate timed out after 5.0s (fail-closed: treat as HELD)` -> `RepairPauseError: Error: doctor repair could not acquire its reconciliation pause`.\nRoot cause: the test runs real git under the production fail-closed bound `_ref_lock._LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS = 5.0`, which a starved host can exceed. The bound is correct product policy; the test's dependence on wall-clock headroom is the defect, and the same defect already hit test_advisory_lock.py (ddc8-5fcf) and test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py (dissocial-malleable-tuna).\n\n**Change** (commit a51ba426bf7, worktree fix-ref-lock-test-bound): `tests/conftest.py` `_give_ref_lock_git_headroom()` sets the bound to 60 s in `pytest_configure`; the two per-module overrides are removed (no `_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS\", 60` monkeypatch remains under tests/). Production source is unchanged.\n\n**New test** `test_a_slow_local_git_call_does_not_fail_the_repair_pause` (every update-ref delayed 5.6 s; asserts the in-flight refusal, no pause left, and that the shim logged at least 2 delayed update-refs):\n- with origin/main's conftest: fails with the timeout above.\n- with the change: 1 passed.\ntest_advisory_lock.py, test_ref_lock.py, test_ref_lock_blob_read_budget.py, test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py, test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py: 66 passed (load average ~33).\n\n**Observation, not acted on:** when the slow call is the cleanup delete rather than the create (the reported run), production leaves the durable pause in place and reports \"left for operator recovery\". That is the designed fail-closed outcome; a slow local git under real load would need operator recovery.","timestamp":1795156333566174001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Same class, second test (coordinator lead from the almondy-drop-acl-step verify, Nov 19-20): tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py::test_pre_pause_decoder_accepts_every_new_pause_blob failed with RefLockTimeoutError on a 'git commit-tree' (via _ref_lock_push.wrap_commit) exceeding _LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS. Reproduced with a PATH shim sleeping 5.6 s before commit-tree: origin/main's conftest -> TimeoutExpired 'timed out after 5.0 seconds' on every parameter; with this change's session headroom -> 3 passed. That lead's rerun.log shows 'no tests ran', so the claim that it still failed serially is not supported by that log.","timestamp":1795180253988949001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local verify evidence (verify-parity sweep, for this ticket's scope): in the 5 sandboxed, oversubscribed make verify runs of Nov 19-20 (about 8 concurrent -n 4 suites), ref-lock 5 s bounds expired (RefLockTimeoutError: git rev-parse --verify / update-ref timed out after 5.0s) and failed: test_reconciler_last_pass (3 tests), reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_entry::test_main_returns_0_when_reconcile_succeeds, test_doctor_dirty_tree (5 tests), test_advisory_lock_cas_race::test_ref_backend_create_cas_single_winner, test_reconcile_cli_state_removal_82bb::test_retired_pause_sentinel_blocks_write_capable_modes, test_ref_lock_lease (4 tests), test_ref_lock_chain::test_writes_over_a_legacy_blob_tip_leave_a_commit. None failed in the 5 complete slot-capped unsandboxed runs. Logs: .rebar/scratch/05f74084-win/verify-willet.log and .rebar/worktrees/{bug-create-replay,fix-janitor-byte-race,fix-test-git-maint-detach}/.rebar/scratch/s05f74084/make-verify.log. Not worked by the sweep.","timestamp":1795206531716795001}],"created_at":1795144803318624001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d12a747a-2809-420a-8cac-50d2174d69fb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ddc8-5fcf-93c4-4406"},{"link_uuid":"878534a8-05be-40a2-b887-09b60e6345e8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d8f6-2168-06e7-4133"},{"link_uuid":"4f387ff9-3ea8-4937-a8a3-952decc3090e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa59-9a21-097b-49be"},{"link_uuid":"16296452-ef72-4279-a4f1-6528c60327e5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3992-da04-bbcd-495d"},{"link_uuid":"db67674a-f13f-4942-b804-a77c75c0a567","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fdba-3477-762d-4b7e"}],"description":"## Observation\nA local `make verify` (worktree w1-koala-goose, test-only change to test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py; host running 3 concurrent verifies, wall time 1:49:19) failed `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py::test_in_flight_refusal_clears_owned_pause_before_mutation[doctor]`: `RefLockTimeoutError: git update-ref refs/reconciler/gate timed out after 5.0s (fail-closed: treat as HELD)`, re-raised as `RepairPauseError: a reconciler pass is in flight`. The suite had 1 failed, 21561 passed. The module then passed 3 times in isolation on the same host (30 passed each, 58 s, 131 s, 135 s).\n\n## Hypothesis (unproven)\nSame class as closed ticket sensible-curt-acouchi: the test fails whenever one local `git update-ref` in its temp repo exceeds `_ref_lock._LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` (5.0 s), which host load can cause. Not yet reproduced deterministically with a delaying git shim for this test.\n\n## Root cause (reproduced deterministically on 2026-11-19)\nThe hypothesis holds. A PATH shim (`git` wrapper that sleeps before any `update-ref`, then runs the real git) on origin/main 2ca3e28fcc6:\n- delay 4.5 s: `test_in_flight_refusal_clears_owned_pause_before_mutation` 2 passed.\n- delay 5.6 s: both parameters fail. `[doctor]` raises `RefLockTimeoutError: git update-ref refs/reconciler/gate timed out after 5.0s (fail-closed: treat as HELD)` from `set_pause`, re-raised as `RepairPauseError: Error: doctor repair could not acquire its reconciliation pause`; `[fsck]` reports the same refusal. In the reported run the slow call was the cleanup delete of the same ref, which takes the same path.\nThe test asserts pause-ownership semantics but runs real git in a temporary repository under the production bound `_ref_lock._LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS = 5.0`, which it does not control. The production behaviour is correct: a local ref operation that takes over 5 s is treated as HELD (fail-closed, ADR policy), and closed bugs sensible-curt-acouchi and dissocial-malleable-tuna kept that bound.\n\n## The class\nThis is the third module to fail this way. sensible-curt-acouchi fixed `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py` and dissocial-malleable-tuna fixed `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py`, each with a per-module `monkeypatch.setattr(_ref_lock, \"_LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS\", 60.0)`. 35 test files drive the ref-lock backend; each one that runs real git is exposed until someone adds the same line after a CI failure.\n\n## Approach\nSet the bound once for the test session instead of per module. In `tests/conftest.py`'s `pytest_configure`, set `rebar.reconciler._ref_lock._LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS = 60.0` (xdist workers run `pytest_configure` too). `_ref_lock` is always reached as that one module object (`_advisory_lock._load_ref_lock` is `importlib.import_module(\"rebar.reconciler._ref_lock\")`), and `_ref_lock_push` reads `core._LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS` at call time, so every in-process caller sees it. Production code is unchanged: the bound stays 5.0 s and a timeout still means HELD. The fail-closed contract stays proven by `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py::test_timeout_raises_reflocktimeout`, which forces `TimeoutExpired` independently of the bound. Remove the two per-module overrides, which the session setting replaces, and point their docstrings at it. This loosens a time bound in test code only; it is recorded here as the prior tickets recorded theirs.\nLimit: a rebar child process started by a test does not inherit an in-process setting; this change covers in-process callers only.\nRejected: raising the production bound (it is a deliberate fail-closed policy); another per-module override (the class reopens with the next module).\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/conftest.py`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`\n\n## Testing\n- Add `test_a_slow_local_git_call_does_not_fail_the_repair_pause` to `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`: with a PATH `git` shim that sleeps 5.6 s before `update-ref` and records each delayed call to a file, run the doctor in-flight path and assert the `a reconciler pass is in flight` refusal, that no pause is left behind, and that the shim recorded at least one delayed `update-ref` (so the test cannot pass without exercising the delay). On the pre-fix tree it fails with the timeout above; with the session setting it passes.\n- `test_advisory_lock.py`'s existing slow-git test keeps passing with its module override removed.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py`, `test_ref_lock_blob_read_budget.py` (it compares recorded budgets to the module attribute), `test_advisory_lock.py`, `test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py`, and `test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py` pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The failure is reproduced deterministically (e.g. a git shim delaying update-ref past 5 s) and the root cause recorded.\n- [ ] The test no longer fails under that reproduction, or the bug is closed with the evidence-backed disposition.\n- [ ] The new slow-git test fails on the pre-fix tree and passes with the change (both runs recorded here).\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"session-wide ref-lock local bound for tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py","reason":"drop per-module override replaced by the session setting"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py","reason":"drop per-module override replaced by the session setting"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py","reason":"slow-git regression test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3992-da04-bbcd-495d"],["relates_to","ddc8-5fcf-93c4-4406"],["relates_to","fa59-9a21-097b-49be"],["relates_to","fdba-3477-762d-4b7e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b8dc744d-b2d1-4712-8bc4-7a78786f4b8c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["flaky","tests"],"ticket_id":"c0ed-53e2-aa14-48f8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Repair-pause in-flight test fails when a git update-ref in its temp repo exceeds the 5-second ref-lock bound under host load","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["314ab5ac-c96d-44ae-b2e0-02a51b4b4f9f","b9cc7743-a0ed-4fc4-a4b8-3e9a6184142c","b6e18c35-8300-41f6-9700-a010fa4b2b73","b8dc744d-b2d1-4712-8bc4-7a78786f4b8c","8130d012-feef-438f-9747-8aa9f38da353","39594425-58aa-40eb-87bb-fcb7c34676ba","ce4f456c-f6a8-430d-a9bb-a55691264272","4f387ff9-3ea8-4937-a8a3-952decc3090e","16296452-ef72-4279-a4f1-6528c60327e5","e9b137ce-c2de-4c9b-b51c-c7730dd77aa2","db67674a-f13f-4942-b804-a77c75c0a567"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795207993826171487,"uuid":"75cc3e03-01bb-4808-8659-b92e0ad2f6e2"}